{'symbol': 'TWTR', 'date': '2019-10-30 22:30:00', 'title': 'ROSEN LAW FIRM ANNOUNCES FILING OF SECURITIES CLASS ACTION LAWSUIT AGAINST TWITTER, INC', 'text': 'ROSEN LAW FIRM ANNOUNCED THE FILING OF A CLASS ACTION LAWSUIT ON BEHALF OF PURCHASERS OF THE SECURITIES OF TWITTER, INC. BETWEEN AUGUST 6, 2019 AND OCTOBER 23, 2019. THE LAWSUIT SEEKS TO RECOVER DAMAGES FOR TWITTER INVESTORS UNDER THE FEDERAL SECURITIES LAWS. ACCORDING TO THE LAWSUIT, DEFENDANTS THROUGHOUT THE CLASS PERIOD MADE FALSE AND/OR MISLEADING STATEMENTS AND/OR FAILED TO DISCLOSE THAT: (1) WHILE TWITTER REPRESENTED THAT IT “FIXED” CERTAIN ISSUES RELATING TO USER CHOICE SETTINGS DESIGNED TO TARGET ADVERTISING WERE NOT WORKING AS INTENDED; (2) THE CHANGES IMPLEMENTED TO FIX THESE ISSUES ADVERSELY AFFECTED TWITTER’S ABILITY TO TARGET ADVERTISING, INCLUDING THE TARGETING OF ADVERTISING THROUGH ITS MOBILE APP PROMOTION (“MAP”) PRODUCT, WHICH CAUSED A MATERIAL DECLINE IN ADVERTISING REVENUE; AND (3) AS A RESULT, TWITTER’S PUBLIC STATEMENTS WERE MATERIALLY FALSE AND MISLEADING AT ALL RELEVANT TIMES. WHEN THE TRUE DETAILS ENTERED THE MARKET, THE LAWSUIT CLAIMS THAT INVESTORS SUFFERED DAMAGES.'}